{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["מרך בלבבם — it is not the idiom of soft-hearted, as in ואל הרך לבי. For the mem of מרך is the root letter, since the vocal stress falls on the mem — as in אהל אוכל בכסף, וקראת לשבת עונג, ואין חבר. Its only parallel is in the Talmud, in Hullin (45b): נתמרך באלו טריפות."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The three unaddressed Hebrew phrases appear to be scriptural or rabbinic illustrations of words where stress on a final/root mem is significant; they are rendered here without addresses as Rashbam cites them. ואין חבר may be an incomplete citation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:30.903322119Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}